Subject: [PATCH] rpm: pass distribution CFLAGS to bundled ksh93 build

The dtksh Makefile invokes the bundled ksh93 package build with CCFLAGS
set only to CDE's SHOPT preprocessor definitions.  This discards the
compiler flags supplied by the RPM build environment.

On Enterprise Linux 9 the linker still receives the distribution
hardening flags and produces PIE executables.  The ksh93 bootstrap
mamake object is therefore compiled without the corresponding compiler
hardening/PIE flags and cannot be linked:

  relocation R_X86_64_32 ... can not be used when making a PIE object

Preserve the ksh93 SHOPT definitions while also passing the configured
CFLAGS into its CCFLAGS variable.

This keeps the distribution hardening policy intact rather than
disabling PIE for the bundled build.
---
diff --git a/cde/programs/dtksh/Makefile.am b/cde/programs/dtksh/Makefile.am
index 52c5990b6..8c0eb60e5 100644
--- a/cde/programs/dtksh/Makefile.am
+++ b/cde/programs/dtksh/Makefile.am
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ dtksh_SOURCES = init.c \
                 msgs.c
 
 ksh93/bin/ksh:
-	ksh93/bin/package flat make CCFLAGS='$(KSH93_SHOPTS)'
+	ksh93/bin/package flat make CCFLAGS='$(CFLAGS) $(KSH93_SHOPTS)'
 
 init.c: ksh93/bin/ksh
 	$(CP) ksh93/src/cmd/ksh93/sh/init.c ./
